## Collection Panel

One card type as a browsable list that runs its own query: a grid, a strip or a table over the same rows, a search box, and an Add button.

```ts
import { CollectionPanel } from '@cardstack/catalog/components/collection-panel';

<CollectionPanel
  @cardClass={{CollectibleProduct}}
  @context={{@context}}
  @realms={{this.realms}}
  @columns={{COLUMNS}}
  @label='Products'
/>
```

The panel takes the card class, not a display name, and asks the realm for that type. `@sortBy` names the field to sort on; it defaults to `title`, and a field the card does not have returns no rows, so a card labelled by another field must pass it. `@extraFilter` is composed into the panel's one query, so the grid, the strip and the table always agree on which rows exist; `@rowFilter` narrows only the resolved table rows. `@allowCreate={{false}}` hides Add for collections whose rows must not be typed in by hand, such as an audit trail.

### Non-goals

It does not edit rows inline or page results.
